+# 111 · A PaymentVoided event joins the sealed PaymentEvent family without its @JsonSubTypes entry
+
+[← All examples](../README.md)
+
+| Verdict | Categories | Severity if shipped | Change | Verified unit | Approach |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **✗ Violation: 1 new problem** | functional | high | feature, behaviour change intended | [`PaymentEvent`](../../examples/apps/boxoffice/contracts/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/boxoffice/contracts/PaymentEvent.java) | [B12: Boundary contracts](../../lib/README.md) |
+
+> The payment service voids an order whose refund arrives before any charge, and until now told nobody. A developer adds a `PaymentVoided` record to the sealed `PaymentEvent` interface, publishes it on the void path, and handles it in ticketing, where the compiler insists on the new case of the sealed switch. The `@JsonSubTypes` list on the interface, which names the type id of each event on the wire, is not touched. Every test passes: the compiler checked the Java side, the codec test round-trips the three events it knew about. Jackson writes the new event with the type id `PaymentEvent$PaymentVoided` and the consumer rejects it. The regenerated boundary contract of the `contracts` module shows the new type with a `!` line saying exactly that.
+
+Tags: [spring-boot](../README.md#tag-spring-boot), [messaging](../README.md#tag-messaging), [payments](../README.md#tag-payments), [dropped-case](../README.md#tag-dropped-case)
+
+## The change
+
+Report a voided payment to ticketing. A refund that overtakes its charge leaves the payment service with a `VOIDED` record and ticketing with an order in `REFUND_PENDING` that waits for a refund of money that was never taken. The payment service now publishes a `PaymentVoided` event on that path, and ticketing settles the order on it as it does on a refund. The new record is added to the sealed `PaymentEvent` interface, so the compiler finds the switch in `PaymentEventHandler` that needs a new case.
+
+**Before** ([`PaymentEvent.java`](../../examples/apps/boxoffice/contracts/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/boxoffice/contracts/PaymentEvent.java), line 24):
+
+```java
+    /** A captured payment was returned to the customer. */
+    record PaymentRefunded(UUID eventId, String orderId, Instant occurredAt, String paymentId, long amountCents)
+            implements PaymentEvent {}
+}
+```
+
+**After:**
+
+```java
+    /** A captured payment was returned to the customer. */
+    record PaymentRefunded(UUID eventId, String orderId, Instant occurredAt, String paymentId, long amountCents)
+            implements PaymentEvent {}
+
+    /**
+     * A refund arrived before any charge, so the order was voided: nothing was captured, and a charge that arrives
+     * later is refused. Reported so that the order does not wait for a refund that will never happen.
+     */
+    record PaymentVoided(UUID eventId, String orderId, Instant occurredAt, String reason) implements PaymentEvent {}
+}
+```
+
